# Lustra — core

Sources of truth: `docs/PRD.md` (what/why), `docs/TECH-DESIGN.md` (how). On conflict, prefer TECH-DESIGN for schema/API.

## File naming

- **Files & folders: `kebab-case` only** — `hold-slot.usecase.ts`, `master-card.tsx`, `booking-status.machine.ts`, `use-hold-timer.ts`.
- React/Nest **symbols** stay PascalCase / camelCase in code (`HoldSlotUseCase`, `MasterCard`) — only the filename is kebab-case.
- Tests colocated: `phone.test.ts` next to `phone.ts`. No `HoldSlotUseCase.ts` / `MasterCard.tsx` filenames.

## Size & composition (hard)

- React component / Nest service / use-case class: **≤ 300 lines**. Split earlier if responsibilities mix.
- Prefer **composition** over inheritance and over mega-files.
- No god objects: one class = one reason to change (SRP). Depend on abstractions (ports/interfaces), not concrete Prisma in domain.

## SOLID (practical)

| Letter | Rule here |
|---|---|
| S | Use-case / component does one job; extract when a second appears |
| O | Extend via new use-case/handler, not by bloating existing service with `if (type === …)` |
| L | Substitutable ports (e.g. `Clock`, repositories) |
| I | Narrow interfaces — don't force callers to depend on unused methods |
| D | Domain/app depend on ports; `infra/` implements Prisma/Redis/HTTP |

## Boundaries

- Frontend never trusts itself for authz or money/time invariants — API is source of truth.
- Backend: private fields (`masterNote`, `trustScore`, `addressExact`) never leak via client DTOs.
- Roles: `client` \| `master` \| `admin`. Resource owner IDs come from JWT/session, **never** from request body.

## Control flow braces (required)

Never write single-line `if` / `else` / `for` / `while` without braces. Always expand for readability:

```ts
// ❌ BAD
if (!master) notFound();

// ✅ GOOD
if (!master) {
  notFound();
}
```

Same for early returns, throws, and one-liner bodies.

## Blank lines (readability)

Always leave a blank line:

- between separate `if` / `else` blocks (not inside a single `if / else if / else` chain)
- between `case` arms in `switch`
- after a loop block when more code follows
- immediately before every `return` (including early returns)

```ts
if (!user) {
  throw new ForbiddenException('Доступ запрещён')
}

if (!roles.includes(user.role)) {
  throw new ForbiddenException('Недостаточно прав')
}

return true
```

## Path aliases (required)

- Use `@/` aliases **everywhere** in `apps/api` and `apps/web` (e.g. `@/modules/master-profile/app/...`).
- Same-folder `./foo` is OK; never `../` across folders.
- API: Nest `compilerOptions.builder = "webpack"` resolves `@/` from `tsconfig` paths.

## Docs / agent

- Before non-trivial features: read relevant TECH-DESIGN § and apply matching `.cursor/skills/`.
- Don't invent parallel architectures (tRPC, thick Express services, Zustand global store).

## Commit message at the end (required)

After **every** completed feature/fix/task, end the reply with a ready-to-use **commit message** (do not create the commit unless the user asked). Format must pass commitlint (Conventional Commits):

```
type(scope): short subject in English or Russian

Optional body — why, not a file list.
```

Types: `feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `perf` `test` `build` `ci` `chore` `revert`.  
Scope examples: `api`, `web`, `landing`, `db`, `ui`, `auth`, `booking`.

Place it last, clearly labeled, e.g.:

**Commit message:**
```
feat(api): add hold-slot use-case
```
